<title>GERMANY: Gold may break higher - bank report.</title>
<headline>Gold may break higher - bank report.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold may be poised to move higher, leaving its current $380-385 an ounce trading range behind, Dresdner Bank said in a weekly precious metals report.</p>
<p>If gold broke overhead resistance at $385 per ounce, followed by $386 and $386.50, it could easily move towards $390, the bank said, citing fund interest.</p>
<p>It recommended cautious buying at the lower end of the current range.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
